                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Who computes the view-factor GEOMETRY of every probe x polygon pair (the cos·area/r² term and its rejects) before the rays — separate from Engine, which picks the ray caster. Auto: the OpenCL GPU when one answers, else the CPU; a fallback is reported in the log and as a warning. CPU: the parallel loop. GPU: refuse to run silently on the CPU. Same answer either way (float geometry on the GPU; measured within 2e-6 per view factor at Reference fidelity).</item>
